# Pure Integration

## Senior Systems Engineer - OSP Design

**Location:** Remote

**Job Type:** Full-Time

**Salary:** $100,000-$120,000

**Posted on:** 05/09/2025

### Job Description

Pure Integration is looking for a highly skilled and motivated Senior Systems Engineer - OSP Design to join our growing team. The ideal candidate is an experienced outside plant (OSP) engineer with a strong background in fiber optic network design, specifically within the cable TV or telecom sector. This role involves managing the design process from conception through permitting and construction, ensuring projects are completed on time, within budget, and in compliance with all relevant regulations.

**Responsibilities:**

* Create and review OSP designs, including fiber distribution, splice mapping, and network topology diagrams
* Develop detailed construction drawings and permits packages
* Conduct field surveys and gather data for network design and permitting purposes
* Work with local municipalities and utility companies to obtain required permits
* Coordinate with project managers and construction teams to deliver projects on schedule
* Review and approve permit applications, ensuring compliance with local regulations
* Assist in the development of design standards and documentation procedures
* Perform quality checks on design documentation and construction drawings
* Stay current with industry trends and technologies

**Requirements:**

* 5-10 years of experience in OSP design and engineering, specifically in the cable or telecom industries
* Proficiency in design tools such as AutoCAD, MicroStation, or similar
* Experience with GIS tools, preferably ArcGIS or similar platforms
* Strong understanding of fiber optic network design, including GPON/XGS-PON architectures
* Knowledge of permitting processes and regulations for both aerial and underground construction
* Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings and construction documents
* Strong project management and communication skills
* Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced environment

**Preferred Qualifications:**

* Experience with design software specific to the cable or telecom industry (e.g., Bentley, QGIS, or similar)
* Familiarity with make-ready engineering and pole attachment requirements
* Experience working with cable TV operators (MSOs) or telcos

